`applicationDidEnterBackground` (or its scene equivalent) is your last reliable checkpoint before iOS may suspend or kill you without further notice. Do the save synchronously and fast — you get seconds, not minutes.

```swift
func applicationDidEnterBackground(_ application: UIApplication) {
    // Flush anything the user would be upset to lose.
    draftStore.saveSynchronously()

    // Persist enough to restore the screen the user was on.
    UserDefaults.standard.set(currentScreenID, forKey: "lastScreen")
}
```

The key discipline: don't defer this to a background task expecting more time later. Treat `didEnterBackground` as your only guaranteed shot — anything async you kick off here can be cut short.
